 ### Triangle-to-Grid Insertion
-A simpler variant that determines overlapped cells by bounding box overlap and adds a triangle reference to each [S2]. It uses bounding box overlap test instead of exact triangle-in-box test. The exact test reduces triangle references by more than one third, but shrinks ray-triangle intersection tests by only a few percent after mailboxing, so the higher rebuild cost of the exact test is not justified [S2]. For scenes with dominantly long, skinny, and diagonal triangles, a more accurate test may still pay off [S2].
