+- **When to use:** When building a sparse voxel DAG for ray tracing or volume rendering where performance is critical and the scene contains varied triangle orientations [G].
 - **When not to use:** For scenes with very long, skinny, diagonal triangles where bounding box overlap is highly inaccurate and exact tests might be justified [S2].
 
 ## Background
-NGLE Triangle Voxelization is part of the Sparse Voxel DAG (SVO) builder implementation found in the INF584 High Resolution Sparse Voxel DAGs project [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the concept of adaptive sparse voxelization with bounding box thickness cases [1686-adaptive-sparse-voxelization-with-bounding-box-thickness-cas]. The method is designed to efficiently rasterize triangles into a sparse grid structure for subsequent ray traversal [S1, unofficial].
